    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="36">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 36</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="68" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXIII. Eac is funden: gif mon hafað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.39"/> spere ofer eaxle, ⁊ hine mon on asnaseð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.40"/>, gielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.41"/> þone wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.42"/> butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.43"/> wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="68" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXIII. Eac is funden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.15"/>: gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.12"/> hafað spere ofer eaxle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.16"/>, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.12"/> hine mon on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.17"/> asnæseð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.18"/>, gilde þone wer buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.12"/> wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="69" ed="#liebermann"/>Be speres gymeleaste. Eac is funden: gyf mon hæfð spere ofer eaxle, ⁊ hine man onsnæseþ, gylde þone wer buton wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="69" ed="#liebermann"/>Inuentum est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.21"/> etiam: si quis habeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.22"/> lanceam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.23"/> super humerum suum, et aliquis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.24"/> (homo) on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.25"/> asnased (uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_36.lnote.oe.26"/> impungatur), soluat weram eius sine wita.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="78" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be speres gymeleaste.] Eac is funden: gif mon hafað<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Af_36.attnote.fn.18"/> spere ofer eaxle<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Af_36.attnote.fn.19"/>, ⁊ hine mon on asnaseð<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Af_36.attnote.fn.20"/>, gielde þone wer butan wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="37" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="332" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXXIII} Eac is funden: gif mon hafað spere ofer eaxle, ⁊ hine mon on asnaseð, gielde þone wer butan wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="69" ed="#liebermann"/>Ferner ist beschlossen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_36.lnote.de.1"/>: wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_36.lnote.de.2"/> jemand den Speer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_36.lnote.de.3"/> über der Achsel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_36.lnote.de.4"/> hat, und sich einer daran spiesst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_36.lnote.de.5"/>, so zahle jener das Wergeld ohne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_36.lnote.de.6"/> Strafgeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Further, it is decided: if someone has his spear over his shoulder, and someone is spitted on it, let the former pay the wergeld without fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="79" ed="#attenborough"/>It is further enacted: if a man has a spear over his shoulder, and anyone is transfixed thereon, he shall pay the wergeld without the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="414" ed="#whitelock"/>Moreover, it is established: if anyone has a spear over his shoulder, and a man is transfixed on it, the wergild is to be paid without the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="333" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Likewise it is determined: if someone has a spear on [his] shoulder, and someone impales himself on it, let him pay the <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>, without a fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="333"><label>foreshadowed in</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-13">Af El 13</ref> <quote>the relevance of intent or its absence is foreshadowed in MP §13</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="413"><label>generalizes</label> <ref target="clause:Hn_88-2">Hn 88.2</ref> <quote>Alfred's law on clumsy spear-carriers ... was prefaced: 'In ... legal proceedings of this kind consideration must be given to the manner of carrying'</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hæfað <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> hæfþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hæfað So; hæfþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">asnæseð <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> onsnæseþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">asnæseð So; onsnæseþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gylde <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> gyld <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gylde Ld; gyld So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.42" n="42" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">were <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">were So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> gefunden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to gefunden</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> eaxlen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to eaxlen</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dabit <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dabit R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">habet <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">habet Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suam <hi rend="italic">fügt zu T Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">suam added by T Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> al. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> homo <hi rend="italic">übrige;</hi> quis <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi> 88, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only al. Lond; only homo the others; quis Hn 88, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Or;</hi> asnasetur [anas. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>] <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Or; asnasetur [anas. Hk] the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. i. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. i. lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Stilistisch ungeschickte Anordnung der Gedanken Ælfreds (<hi rend="italic">s.</hi> 36, 2¹) erschwerte Früheren die Auslegung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The stylistically clumsy arrangement of Ælfred’s ideas (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> 36, 2¹) made interpretation difficult for earlier scholars</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Keineswegs ein bei Hofe damals wohl bekanntes Ereignis brauchte zu diesem Gesetz den Anlass zu geben. Denn Friesenrecht bietet Ähnliches; <hi rend="italic">L. Fris. Add.</hi> III 69</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It need by no means have been some event well known at court at the time that gave occasion to this law. For Frisian law offers something similar; <hi rend="italic">L. Fris. Add.</hi> III 69</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Speer 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Speer 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Geschultert, mit der Spitze nach hinten. Verwundung hinter dem Rücken gilt ohne Absicht (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5a) auch Friesisch; Wilda <hi rend="italic">Strafr.</hi> 549</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Carried on the shoulder, with the point to the rear. Wounding behind the back counts as unintentional (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5a) in Frisian law too; Wilda <hi rend="italic">Strafr.</hi> 549</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> behielt die Agsä. Wörter, weil noch unverstanden, bei</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> retained the Anglo-Saxon words because they were not yet understood</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_36.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bei kasueller Tötung (Frank <hi rend="italic">Casu. Töt.</hi> 59) bedarf es keines Gefährdeeides zum Fortfalle des Friedensgeldes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the case of accidental killing (Frank <hi rend="italic">Casu. Töt.</hi> 59) no oath denying intent is needed for the peace-money to fall away</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_36.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope></bibl><label>hafað</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hæfð</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_36.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope></bibl><label>eaxle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">eaxlen</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_36.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope></bibl><label>asnaseð</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">onsnæseð</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">on asnæseð</hi>. H.</seg></note>
